# GO-2026-5932: golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp flagged as unmaintained/unsafe by
# design (no fixed version — deprecated package, not a patched CVE).
#
# x/crypto is pulled in transitively via github.com/go-sprout/sprout
# (template.go:12, template.go:41 -- sprigin.TxtFuncMap() backs gossfile
# templating), which needs x/crypto/bcrypt, not openpgp. The openpgp
# subpackage itself is not reachable from goss's build graph (verified with
# `go list -deps ./...`).
#
# Re-verify on every commit that touches go.mod/go.sum or this file:
# ci/trivyignore-check.sh (wired into .githooks/pre-commit) flags any entry
# below whose underlying scan result has changed (fixed version shipped,
# ID no longer present, or reachability changed) so it can be re-evaluated
# instead of silently going stale.
GO-2026-5932
